    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The neighborhood sits in Oakland’s foothills, bordered by MacArthur Boulevard, High Street, Trask Street, Foothill Boulevard, and 55th Avenue, and neighbors Mills College and Fairfax.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maxwell_Park%2C_Oakland%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Many homes in Maxwell Park overlook the Oakland Hills to the north, Alameda to the east, and the San Francisco Bay to the west.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maxwell_Park%2C_Oakland%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The original development area was bounded by 55th Avenue, Trask Street, Monticello Avenue, and Camden Street.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maxwell_Park%2C_Oakland%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Maxwell Park itself stretches from Fleming Avenue to Allendale Avenue between High Street and Monticello Avenue, and features mosaic‑adorned restrooms and chess tables.",
